{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$X = \\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pf-flat-module-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0ee636a9e0f1f3c48329209b63a64ded9e4ea6d2e77f70f38fe8ad1d62e7e050", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4a46ba3f9d2312c4e64eb9c90afc7fba5016d4a4ffd39c56d612caaf57a8481", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nAssume <MATH_0004> locally finite presentation, <MATH_0005> of\nfinite type, <MATH_0006>, and\n<MATH_0007> flat over <MATH_0008>. Then <MATH_0009> is universally open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ae2765a57009262843886f8638b6f53b75c08ba6554798e43e560742ab2d366b", "unit_id": "tag:0CVT:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-module-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-presentation}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-support-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-universally-open}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-going-down-flat-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e01e21ab7152b25d39c390a1508ba79a9521732b95648d8ce334871ab82510c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:65464e662a3dcc75c30b3389b960e2a70182adae27cced47bfb16b6559955a7d", "source_text": "By Lemmas <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>\nthe assumptions are preserved under base change.\nBy Lemma <REF_0004>\nit suffices to show that generalizations lift along <MATH_0001>.\nThis follows from Algebra, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4429fac523969ab5d7633088bd4dca6db450dabff1910d528aeea9cb542d79d2", "unit_id": "tag:0CVT:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[Expose VIII, Corollaire 4.3]{SGA1} and\n\\cite[IV, Corollaire 2.3.12]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}(T)$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fpqc-quotient-topology}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34c07d7f2c0d0ceaf504f5282b7f81f698aa0603104a87421d923ef4a85ed47b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:612722951dea2b0d0b473fa367a41e001b29f379c00990052dee09e0ed2c0307", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact, surjective, flat morphism.\nA subset <MATH_0002> is open (resp.<SPACE_0001>closed) if and only\n<MATH_0003> is open (resp.<SPACE_0002>closed). In other words, <MATH_0004> is\na submersive morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c858306940330fffff97c069e745b5c4a9430eb83947133b21fd1cb58b4d6fc4", "unit_id": "tag:02JY:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01U2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$X = X_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup X_n$", "MATH_0006": "$f' : X' = X_1 \\amalg \\ldots \\amalg X_n \\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\subset Y$", "MATH_0008": "$(f')^{-1}(T) = f^{-1}(T) \\cap X_1 \\amalg \\ldots \\amalg f^{-1}(T) \\cap X_n$", "MATH_0009": "$f^{-1}(T)$", "MATH_0010": "$(f')^{-1}(T)$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$Y$", "MATH_0013": "$f : \\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0014": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0015": "$f^{-1}(T)$", "MATH_0016": "$f^{-1}(T) = V(J)$", "MATH_0017": "$J \\subset B$", "MATH_0018": "$T = f(f^{-1}(T)) = f(V(J))$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Spec(B/J) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0020": "$f$", "MATH_0021": "$f$", "MATH_0022": "$Y \\setminus T = f(X \\setminus f^{-1}(T))$", "MATH_0023": "$T$", "MATH_0024": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-generalizations-lift-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-lift-specializations-images}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-lemma-open-closed-specialization}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-image-stable-specialization-closed}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fbf0b7ab42f89cf0ebb8529904c2fd9a55ecdcfa34947dacc231799be4a07f58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db92882560a1fd0531f6f54c4e9feb2cf3bbf83a93ff465db7b7eef71fe75eb0", "source_text": "The question is local on <MATH_0001>, hence we may assume that <MATH_0002> is affine.\nIn this case <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact as <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\nWrite <MATH_0005> as a finite union of affine opens.\nThen <MATH_0006> is a surjective\nflat morphism of affine schemes. Note that for <MATH_0007> we have\n<MATH_0008>.\nHence, <MATH_0009> is open if and only if <MATH_0010> is open.\nThus we may assume both <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> are affine.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0013> be a surjective morphism of affine schemes\ncorresponding to a flat ring map <MATH_0014>. Suppose that <MATH_0015> is\nclosed, say <MATH_0016> for <MATH_0017> an ideal. Then\n<MATH_0018> is the image of <MATH_0019>\n(here we use that <MATH_0020> is surjective). On the other hand, generalizations\nlift along <MATH_0021> (Lemma <REF_0001>).\nHence by Topology, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0022> is stable under\ngeneralization. Hence <MATH_0023> is stable under specialization\n(Topology, Lemma <REF_0003>).\nThus <MATH_0024> is closed by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b068cb02d0db0931e6efd0383bde220df6ea3f36c1a2beb4ec97362b691d606f", "unit_id": "tag:02JY:proof"}
